//! member: false
//!
//! uniq — filter ADJACENT matching lines.
//!
//! References consulted: POSIX.1-2024 `uniq`; GNU coreutils 9.11's
//! `uniq --help`, the info manual's option descriptions, and black-box
//! runs of the GNU binary on macOS arm64 (Homebrew `guniq`) and linux
//! x86-64 (native `uniq`), under `LC_ALL=C`; uutils/coreutils (MIT) and
//! toybox (0BSD) as design references for the shape of a group loop.
//! Never GNU source.
//!
//! **Adjacent, and only adjacent.** `uniq` never sorts and never
//! remembers a line it has left behind: `a b a` is three groups, not
//! two, and `uniq` prints `a b a`. It is the most common misconception
//! about this utility and the corpus says so in a case of its own.
//!
//! GNU's rules, each measured against coreutils 9.11 on BOTH hosts,
//! which agreed on every case below:
//!
//! - **Three switches, not one mode.** A group of N equal lines prints
//!   its first line when N is 1 and `unique` is on, or when N is more
//!   than 1 and `first_rep` is on; it prints lines 2..N when
//!   `later_rep` is on. `-d` clears `unique`; `-u` clears `first_rep`;
//!   `-D` clears `unique` and sets `later_rep`. That is why `-d -u`
//!   prints NOTHING and `-D -u` prints every line of every repeating
//!   group except its first.
//! - **Equality is an equivalence**, because the comparison is a key
//!   (skip some fields, skip some characters, take at most so many,
//!   fold case). So comparing each line against the group's FIRST line
//!   answers exactly what comparing it against the line before it does,
//!   and one line of state is enough.
//! - **`-c` is seven columns then one space**, widening rather than
//!   truncating past 9,999,999.
//! - **`-c` with `-D` is refused**; `--group` is refused beside any of
//!   `-c`, `-d`, `-D` and `-u`.
//! - **The group separators are two different rules.**
//!   `--all-repeated=prepend` writes a blank line before every group it
//!   prints and `=separate` between them. `--group` writes one before
//!   every group (`prepend`), between them (`separate`), after every
//!   group (`append`), or before the first, between, and after the last
//!   (`both`) — which is NOT "prepend and append", because the blank
//!   between two groups is never doubled.
//! - **A field is a run of blanks then a run of non-blanks**, and
//!   fields are skipped before characters. Either skip may run off the
//!   end of the line, which leaves nothing to compare, so every line
//!   then matches every other.
//! - **The obsolete `-N` is still live**: `-1` skips one field, and
//!   consecutive digit options ACCUMULATE, so `-1 -2` is twelve, while
//!   any other option between them starts the number again.
//! - **The delimiter is always written**, so an input whose last line
//!   has none still gets one, and `-z` ends every record with a NUL.
//! - **The operands are INPUT then OUTPUT**, and a third is an error.
//!   An input that cannot be opened is `uniq: NAME: reason` with NAME
//!   quoted only when it must be; an input that opens and then fails to
//!   read — a directory — is `uniq: error reading 'NAME': reason`, with
//!   NAME always quoted.
//! - Usage errors exit 1 (not 2), as bu00 measured for this family.
//!
//! **The obsolete `+N` is NOT implemented, and it cannot be.** GNU's
//! `+N` (skip N characters) is gated on a BUILD-TIME setting, not on
//! the release: at the same coreutils 9.11, Arch's native `uniq` reads
//! `uniq +1` as the obsolete skip and Homebrew's `guniq` reads it as a
//! file operand and reports `+1: No such file or directory`. No one
//! answer matches both hosts, so boreutils takes the POSIX one — `+1`
//! is a file name — and the corpus records the divergence in a skipped
//! case rather than pinning either host's build.
//!
//! **`--group` and `--all-repeated` take an OPTIONAL argument**, which
//! `bore.parse` cannot express: its options either take an argument or
//! they do not. A bare `--group` is rewritten here to `--group=` before
//! parsing, which is the same thing to `bore.parse` and stops
//! `uniq --group FILE` eating FILE as the argument. Reported to the
//! wave rather than fixed in `bore`, which bu05 owns this wave.
//!
//! **Memory, and the one wolf construct this program needed.**
//! `fs_read_chunk` allocates the list it answers and the ambient region
//! frees none of it (wolf-lang#416), so every chunk is read inside
//! `region pass`. What must outlive the chunk — the first line of the
//! open group, and the partial line at a chunk boundary — lives in a
//! FIRST-CLASS region opened once (`let keep = region()`) and is
//! written through `in keep { }`. That is the only way at 0.2.14 to
//! carry a value across a dying region, and both buffers are
//! overwritten in place rather than rebuilt, so `keep` grows to the
//! longest line seen and no further. Output is built in a region-local
//! buffer and written with `bore.write_direct`, because a `mut`
//! parameter that lives OUTSIDE the block is E1010 at any call made
//! inside it.

use bore

/// What was asked for.
struct Conf {
    count: bool,
    unique: bool,
    first_rep: bool,
    later_rep: bool,
    all_repeated: bool,
    ignore_case: bool,
    delim: int,
    skip_fields: int,
    skip_chars: int,
    check_chars: int,
    /// -1 off, else 0 separate, 1 prepend, 2 append, 3 both.
    group: int,
    /// `--all-repeated`: 0 none, 1 prepend, 2 separate.
    method: int,
}

/// The bytes one read asks for.
fn chunk() -> int {
    1048576
}

/// The largest skip or width this program holds. GNU clamps a huge
/// count to SIZE_MAX and never reports it; wolf's arithmetic is
/// checked, so the clamp has to be written down.
fn cap() -> int {
    1000000000
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------- the numbers

/// `text` as a count, or -1 when it is not one. Digits only: GNU's
/// reader takes no sign and no space here, and clamps rather than
/// failing on a number too large to hold.
pub fn to_count(text: str) -> int {
    if text.len == 0 {
        return -1
    }
    var v = 0
    for c in text.chars() {
        let d = c as int - 48
        if d < 0 || d > 9 {
            return -1
        }
        if v < cap() {
            v = v * 10 + d
        }
        if v > cap() {
            v = cap()
        }
    }
    v
}

// ----------------------------------------------------------- comparing

fn is_blank(b: byte) -> bool {
    let n = b as int
    n == 32 || n == 9
}

fn fold(n: int, ignore_case: bool) -> int {
    if ignore_case && n >= 65 && n <= 90 {
        return n + 32
    }
    n
}

/// Where the comparison starts in the window `line[from..to]`, given the
/// field and character skips.
///
/// A WINDOW, not a whole list, because a line is read where it lies: in
/// the chunk it arrived in, and in the carry-over buffer only when it
/// straddled a boundary. The streaming lane measured that copying each
/// line out first is the expensive shape, and this is the other one.
pub fn key_start(line: List[byte], from: int, to: int, skip_fields: int, skip_chars: int) -> int {
    var i = from
    var f = 0
    while f < skip_fields && i < to {
        while i < to && is_blank(line[i]) {
            i += 1
        }
        while i < to && !is_blank(line[i]) {
            i += 1
        }
        f += 1
    }
    var k = 0
    while k < skip_chars && i < to {
        i += 1
        k += 1
    }
    i
}

/// Where the comparison ends.
fn key_end(start: int, to: int, check_chars: int) -> int {
    if check_chars < 0 {
        return to
    }
    var e = start + check_chars
    if e > to {
        e = to
    }
    e
}

/// Whether two line windows compare equal under `c`.
fn same(a: List[byte], afrom: int, ato: int, b: List[byte], bfrom: int, bto: int, c: Conf) -> bool {
    let astart = key_start(a, afrom, ato, c.skip_fields, c.skip_chars)
    let bstart = key_start(b, bfrom, bto, c.skip_fields, c.skip_chars)
    let aend = key_end(astart, ato, c.check_chars)
    let bend = key_end(bstart, bto, c.check_chars)
    if aend - astart != bend - bstart {
        return false
    }
    var i = 0
    while astart + i < aend {
        if fold(a[astart + i] as int, c.ignore_case) != fold(b[bstart + i] as int, c.ignore_case) {
            return false
        }
        i += 1
    }
    true
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------- formatting

fn spaces(n: int) -> str {
    let pad = "       "
    if n <= 0 {
        return ""
    }
    if n >= pad.len {
        return pad
    }
    pad[0..n]
}

/// The `-c` prefix: the count right-aligned in seven columns, then one
/// space, widening rather than truncating.
pub fn counted(n: int) -> str {
    let s = "{n}"
    "{spaces(7 - s.len)}{s} "
}

/// Append one output line, read from the window it lies in, to a
/// region-local buffer.
fn emit(mut buf: List[byte], prefix: str, line: List[byte], from: int, to: int, delim: int) {
    for b in prefix.bytes() {
        (mut buf).push(b)
    }
    var i = from
    while i < to {
        (mut buf).push(line[i])
        i += 1
    }
    (mut buf).push(delim as byte)
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------- the options

fn options() -> List[bore.Opt] {
    var s = List[bore.Opt]()
    (mut s).push(bore.flag("c", "count"))
    (mut s).push(bore.flag("d", "repeated"))
    (mut s).push(bore.flag("D", ""))
    (mut s).push(bore.takes("", "all-repeated"))
    (mut s).push(bore.takes("f", "skip-fields"))
    (mut s).push(bore.takes("", "group"))
    (mut s).push(bore.flag("i", "ignore-case"))
    (mut s).push(bore.takes("s", "skip-chars"))
    (mut s).push(bore.flag("u", "unique"))
    (mut s).push(bore.flag("z", "zero-terminated"))
    (mut s).push(bore.takes("w", "check-chars"))
    (mut s).push(bore.flag("", "help"))
    (mut s).push(bore.flag("", "version"))
    let digits = "0123456789"
    var d = 0
    while d < 10 {
        (mut s).push(bore.flag(digits[d..d + 1], ""))
        d += 1
    }
    s
}

/// Rewrite a bare `--group` or `--all-repeated` — or any prefix of
/// either — as `--NAME=`, so `bore.parse` reads it as an option with an
/// empty argument rather than eating the next operand.
///
/// No other long option of `uniq` starts with `g` or `a`, so a prefix
/// that matches one of these two matches nothing else and the rewrite
/// cannot change what an ambiguous spelling means.
pub fn fix_optional(args: List[str]) -> List[str] {
    var out = List[str]()
    var done = false
    for a in args {
        if done {
            (mut out).push(a)
            continue
        }
        if a == "--" {
            done = true
            (mut out).push(a)
            continue
        }
        if !a.starts_with("--") || a.len == 2 || a.contains("=") {
            (mut out).push(a)
            continue
        }
        let name = a[2..]
        if "group".starts_with(name) || "all-repeated".starts_with(name) {
            (mut out).push("{a}=")
        } else {
            (mut out).push(a)
        }
    }
    out
}

/// `--group`'s method, or -1 when the word names none.
pub fn group_method(v: str) -> int {
    if v.len == 0 || v == "separate" {
        return 0
    }
    if v == "prepend" {
        return 1
    }
    if v == "append" {
        return 2
    }
    if v == "both" {
        return 3
    }
    -1
}

/// `--all-repeated`'s method, or -1.
pub fn repeated_method(v: str) -> int {
    if v.len == 0 || v == "none" {
        return 0
    }
    if v == "prepend" {
        return 1
    }
    if v == "separate" {
        return 2
    }
    -1
}

fn group_words() -> str {
    "Valid arguments are:\n  - 'prepend'\n  - 'append'\n  - 'separate'\n  - 'both'"
}

fn repeated_words() -> str {
    "Valid arguments are:\n  - 'none'\n  - 'prepend'\n  - 'separate'"
}

// ------------------------------------------------------------- the main

fn main() -> int {
    let p = bore.parse(options(), fix_optional(env_args()), bore.permute())
    var c = Conf {
        count: false,
        unique: true,
        first_rep: true,
        later_rep: false,
        all_repeated: false,
        ignore_case: false,
        delim: 10,
        skip_fields: 0,
        skip_chars: 0,
        check_chars: -1,
        group: -1,
        method: 0,
    }
    var saw_c = false
    var saw_d = false
    var saw_dd = false
    var saw_u = false
    var help = false
    var version = false
    var digits_run = false
    var bad = ""
    var i = 0
    while i < p.keys.len {
        let k = p.keys[i]
        let v = p.values[i]
        var is_digit = false
        if k.len == 1 {
            let d = to_count(k)
            if d >= 0 {
                is_digit = true
                if digits_run {
                    if c.skip_fields < cap() {
                        c.skip_fields = c.skip_fields * 10 + d
                    }
                    if c.skip_fields > cap() {
                        c.skip_fields = cap()
                    }
                } else {
                    c.skip_fields = d
                }
                digits_run = true
            }
        }
        if !is_digit {
            digits_run = false
            if k == "help" {
                help = true
            } else if k == "version" {
                version = true
            } else if k == "count" {
                c.count = true
                saw_c = true
            } else if k == "repeated" {
                c.unique = false
                saw_d = true
            } else if k == "D" {
                c.unique = false
                c.later_rep = true
                c.all_repeated = true
                saw_dd = true
            } else if k == "all-repeated" {
                let m = repeated_method(v)
                if m < 0 {
                    return bore.usage_error(
                        "uniq",
                        "invalid argument {bore.quote(v)} for '--all-repeated'\n{repeated_words()}",
                    )
                }
                c.unique = false
                c.later_rep = true
                c.all_repeated = true
                c.method = m
                saw_dd = true
            } else if k == "unique" {
                c.first_rep = false
                saw_u = true
            } else if k == "ignore-case" {
                c.ignore_case = true
            } else if k == "zero-terminated" {
                c.delim = 0
            } else if k == "group" {
                let m = group_method(v)
                if m < 0 {
                    return bore.usage_error(
                        "uniq",
                        "invalid argument {bore.quote(v)} for '--group'\n{group_words()}",
                    )
                }
                c.group = m
            } else if k == "skip-fields" {
                let n = to_count(v)
                if n < 0 && bad.len == 0 {
                    bad = "{v}: invalid number of fields to skip"
                }
                if n >= 0 {
                    c.skip_fields = n
                }
            } else if k == "skip-chars" {
                let n = to_count(v)
                if n < 0 && bad.len == 0 {
                    bad = "{v}: invalid number of bytes to skip"
                }
                if n >= 0 {
                    c.skip_chars = n
                }
            } else if k == "check-chars" {
                let n = to_count(v)
                if n < 0 && bad.len == 0 {
                    bad = "{v}: invalid number of bytes to compare"
                }
                if n >= 0 {
                    c.check_chars = n
                }
            }
        }
        i += 1
    }
    if help || version {
        var h = bore.stdout()
        if help {
            bore.put(mut h, help_text()) else |_| {}
        } else {
            bore.put(mut h, bore.version_text("uniq")) else |_| {}
        }
        return bore.finish(mut h, "uniq", 0)
    }
    if !bore.ok(p) {
        return bore.usage_error("uniq", p.error)
    }
    if bad.len > 0 {
        bore.warn("uniq", bad)
        return 1
    }
    if saw_c && saw_dd {
        return bore.usage_error(
            "uniq",
            "printing all duplicated lines and repeat counts is meaningless",
        )
    }
    if c.group >= 0 && (saw_c || saw_d || saw_dd || saw_u) {
        return bore.usage_error("uniq", "--group is mutually exclusive with -c/-d/-D/-u")
    }
    if p.operands.len > 2 {
        return bore.usage_error("uniq", "extra operand {bore.quote(p.operands[2])}")
    }

    // The sink is opened before the source: with descriptor 1 closed a
    // file opened first takes it (wolf-lang#405).
    var out = bore.stdout()
    if p.operands.len == 2 && p.operands[1] != "-" {
        let target = p.operands[1]
        let fd = fs_open_mode(target, 1) else |e| match e {
            not_found => {
                bore.input_error("uniq", target, bore.no_such_file())
                return 1
            },
            denied => {
                bore.input_error("uniq", target, bore.permission_denied())
                return 1
            },
            exists => {
                bore.input_error("uniq", target, bore.io_error())
                return 1
            },
            invalid => {
                bore.input_error("uniq", target, bore.directory_reason())
                return 1
            },
            io => {
                bore.input_error("uniq", target, bore.directory_reason())
                return 1
            },
        }
        out = bore.Out { fd: fd, direct: true, closed: false, wrote: false, buf: List[byte]() }
    }
    var name = "-"
    if p.operands.len >= 1 {
        name = p.operands[0]
    }
    let src = bore.open_input(name) else |e| match e {
        not_found => {
            bore.input_error("uniq", name, bore.no_such_file())
            return 1
        },
        denied => {
            bore.input_error("uniq", name, bore.permission_denied())
            return 1
        },
        is_dir => {
            // GNU opens a directory and fails on the READ, which is a
            // different message with a differently quoted name.
            bore.warn("uniq", "error reading {bore.quote(name)}: {bore.directory_reason()}")
            return 1
        },
        io => {
            bore.warn("uniq", "error reading {bore.quote(name)}: {bore.io_error()}")
            return 1
        },
    }
    let status = filter(out, src, c)
    bore.close_input(src)
    status
}

/// Read every line and write what the switches ask for.
///
/// Every scalar of the group state lives in this frame and is written
/// straight from inside the blocks; nothing that allocates crosses one,
/// which is why the separator and emission logic is spelled out here
/// rather than handed to helpers taking `mut` parameters from outside.
fn filter(out: bore.Out, src: bore.In, c: Conf) -> int {
    let keep = region()
    var first = List[byte]()
    var pending = List[byte]()
    in keep {
        first = List[byte]()
        pending = List[byte]()
    }
    var first_len = 0
    var pending_len = 0
    var have = false
    var count = 0
    var printed = 0
    var any = false
    var failed = false
    var read_failed = false
    var stop = false
    while !stop {
        region pass {
            let piece = bore.read_chunk(src, chunk()) else |err| match err {
                eof => { stop = true; List[byte]() },
                io => {
                    stop = true
                    read_failed = true
                    List[byte]()
                },
            }
            if piece.len == 0 {
                stop = true
            }
            var buf = List[byte]()
            var at = 0
            var k = 0
            while k < piece.len {
                if piece[k] as int == c.delim {
                    // A line that straddled the boundary finishes in the
                    // carry-over buffer; every other line is compared and
                    // written where it lies, with no copy at all.
                    var from = at
                    var to = k
                    let straddled = pending_len > 0
                    if straddled {
                        in keep {
                            var j = at
                            while j < k {
                                if pending_len < pending.len {
                                    pending[pending_len] = piece[j]
                                } else {
                                    (mut pending).push(piece[j])
                                }
                                pending_len += 1
                                j += 1
                            }
                        }
                        from = 0
                        to = pending_len
                    }
                    let n = to - from
                    var opens = true
                    if have {
                        if straddled {
                            if same(first, 0, first_len, pending, from, to, c) {
                                opens = false
                            }
                        } else if same(first, 0, first_len, piece, from, to, c) {
                            opens = false
                        }
                    }
                    if !opens {
                        count += 1
                    }
                    if opens {
                        if have && !c.all_repeated && c.group < 0 {
                            var show = c.first_rep
                            if count == 1 {
                                show = c.unique
                            }
                            if show {
                                var prefix = ""
                                if c.count {
                                    prefix = counted(count)
                                }
                                emit(mut buf, prefix, first, 0, first_len, c.delim)
                            }
                        }
                        in keep {
                            var t = 0
                            while t < n {
                                var v = 0 as byte
                                if straddled {
                                    v = pending[from + t]
                                } else {
                                    v = piece[from + t]
                                }
                                if t < first.len {
                                    first[t] = v
                                } else {
                                    (mut first).push(v)
                                }
                                t += 1
                            }
                        }
                        first_len = n
                        have = true
                        count = 1
                        if c.group >= 0 {
                            if !any && (c.group == 1 || c.group == 3) {
                                (mut buf).push(c.delim as byte)
                            }
                            if any && (c.group == 2 || c.group == 3) {
                                (mut buf).push(c.delim as byte)
                            }
                            if any && (c.group == 0 || c.group == 1) {
                                (mut buf).push(c.delim as byte)
                            }
                            any = true
                            emit(mut buf, "", first, 0, first_len, c.delim)
                        }
                    } else if c.all_repeated {
                        if count == 2 {
                            if printed == 0 && c.method == 1 {
                                (mut buf).push(c.delim as byte)
                            }
                            if printed > 0 && (c.method == 1 || c.method == 2) {
                                (mut buf).push(c.delim as byte)
                            }
                            printed += 1
                            if c.first_rep {
                                emit(mut buf, "", first, 0, first_len, c.delim)
                            }
                        }
                        if c.later_rep {
                            if straddled {
                                emit(mut buf, "", pending, from, to, c.delim)
                            } else {
                                emit(mut buf, "", piece, from, to, c.delim)
                            }
                        }
                    } else if c.group >= 0 {
                        if straddled {
                            emit(mut buf, "", pending, from, to, c.delim)
                        } else {
                            emit(mut buf, "", piece, from, to, c.delim)
                        }
                    }
                    if straddled {
                        pending_len = 0
                    }
                    at = k + 1
                }
                k += 1
            }
            if at < piece.len {
                in keep {
                    var j = at
                    while j < piece.len {
                        if pending_len < pending.len {
                            pending[pending_len] = piece[j]
                        } else {
                            (mut pending).push(piece[j])
                        }
                        pending_len += 1
                        j += 1
                    }
                }
            }
            if buf.len > 0 {
                bore.write_direct(out, buf) else |_| {
                    failed = true
                    stop = true
                }
            }
        }
    }
    // A last line with no delimiter is still a line, and then the group
    // that is still open has to be closed.
    region tail {
        var buf = List[byte]()
        if pending_len > 0 {
            var opens = true
            if have && same(first, 0, first_len, pending, 0, pending_len, c) {
                opens = false
                count += 1
            }
            if opens {
                if have && !c.all_repeated && c.group < 0 {
                    var show = c.first_rep
                    if count == 1 {
                        show = c.unique
                    }
                    if show {
                        var prefix = ""
                        if c.count {
                            prefix = counted(count)
                        }
                        emit(mut buf, prefix, first, 0, first_len, c.delim)
                    }
                }
                in keep {
                    var t = 0
                    while t < pending_len {
                        if t < first.len {
                            first[t] = pending[t]
                        } else {
                            (mut first).push(pending[t])
                        }
                        t += 1
                    }
                }
                first_len = pending_len
                have = true
                count = 1
                if c.group >= 0 {
                    if !any && (c.group == 1 || c.group == 3) {
                        (mut buf).push(c.delim as byte)
                    }
                    if any && (c.group == 2 || c.group == 3) {
                        (mut buf).push(c.delim as byte)
                    }
                    if any && (c.group == 0 || c.group == 1) {
                        (mut buf).push(c.delim as byte)
                    }
                    any = true
                    emit(mut buf, "", first, 0, first_len, c.delim)
                }
            } else if c.all_repeated {
                if count == 2 {
                    if printed == 0 && c.method == 1 {
                        (mut buf).push(c.delim as byte)
                    }
                    if printed > 0 && (c.method == 1 || c.method == 2) {
                        (mut buf).push(c.delim as byte)
                    }
                    printed += 1
                    if c.first_rep {
                        emit(mut buf, "", first, 0, first_len, c.delim)
                    }
                }
                if c.later_rep {
                    emit(mut buf, "", pending, 0, pending_len, c.delim)
                }
            } else if c.group >= 0 {
                emit(mut buf, "", pending, 0, pending_len, c.delim)
            }
        }
        if have && !c.all_repeated && c.group < 0 {
            var show = c.first_rep
            if count == 1 {
                show = c.unique
            }
            if show {
                var prefix = ""
                if c.count {
                    prefix = counted(count)
                }
                emit(mut buf, prefix, first, 0, first_len, c.delim)
            }
        }
        if c.group >= 0 && any && (c.group == 2 || c.group == 3) {
            (mut buf).push(c.delim as byte)
        }
        if buf.len > 0 {
            bore.write_direct(out, buf) else |_| {
                failed = true
            }
        }
    }
    if read_failed {
        bore.warn("uniq", "read error")
        return 1
    }
    if failed {
        // Streaming through `bore.write_direct` cannot mark the writer
        // as written to, so `bore.finish` would answer 0 here; the
        // failure is reported once, in GNU's wording, instead.
        bore.write_error(out, "uniq", "write error")
        return 1
    }
    0
}

fn help_text() -> str {
    """
    Usage: uniq [OPTION]... [INPUT [OUTPUT]]
    Write INPUT (or standard input) to OUTPUT (or standard output) with
    ADJACENT matching lines merged. Lines that match but do not sit next
    to each other are left alone; sort the input first if that is not
    what you want.

      -c, --count           prefix each line by how many times it ran
      -d, --repeated        print only a line that repeats, once
      -D                    print every line of every repeating group
          --all-repeated[=METHOD]
                            like -D, separating groups: none, prepend or
                            separate
      -f, --skip-fields=N   do not compare the first N fields
          --group[=METHOD]  print every line, separating groups:
                            separate, prepend, append or both
      -i, --ignore-case     compare without regard to case
      -s, --skip-chars=N    do not compare the first N characters
      -u, --unique          print only a line that does not repeat
      -z, --zero-terminated the delimiter is NUL, not newline
      -w, --check-chars=N   compare no more than N characters
          --help            print this help and exit
          --version         print the version and exit

    A field is a run of blanks and then a run of non-blanks. Fields are
    skipped before characters.

    boreutils: https://github.com/wolffe-lang/boreutils
    """
}
